    {
      "id": "nature",
      "text": "Number five: wild nature. Japan is a chain of thousands of islands. Snowy Hokkaido sits in the north, the main island Honshu in the middle, Kyushu in the south, and subtropical Okinawa far to the south-west. Rising above it all is Mount Fuji, a volcano three thousand seven hundred and seventy-six metres high.",
