    {
      "id": "history",
      "text": "Number four: a deep history. Kyoto became the imperial capital in seven ninety-four and stayed that way for more than a thousand years. In sixteen oh three, the Tokugawa shoguns began more than two centuries of peace. Then the Meiji Restoration of eighteen sixty-eight opened Japan to the world, and changed it forever.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "timeline",
        "chapter": "Deep history",
        "rank": 4,
        "events": [
          [
            "794",
            "Kyoto becomes capital"
          ],
          [
            "1603",
            "Tokugawa era begins"
          ],
          [
            "1868",
            "Meiji Restoration"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heritage",
      "text": "And that past is still everywhere you look. Kyoto has more than a thousand temples. Nara is home to famous friendly deer that bow to visitors. Himeji has a gleaming white castle, and in Kamakura a giant bronze Buddha has sat in the open air for centuries.",
